  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member upgrading from the legacy app, I want my accounts imported from the legacy Keychain archive without the app instantiating arbitrary classes, so that the import stays safe without breaking. #1200 P4 tried that and had to be reverted: this issue carries it until a Mac check says which classes the archive really holds.\n\n### What happened\n\n- `LegacyAccountArchive.decode` (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/LegacyImport/KeychainLegacyAccountSource.swift`) reads the `HFR_COMPTES_KEY` item with `requiresSecureCoding = false`, as legacy's `unarchiveObjectWithData:` did (`MultisManager.m:43-47`).\n- #1202 (`27f44e6`) switched to `requiresSecureCoding = true` with `decodeObject(of:)` limited to arrays and mutable arrays, dictionaries and mutable dictionaries, strings and mutable strings, numbers, data and mutable data, dates, URLs and `HTTPCookie`.\n- **Measured**: on macOS, `LegacyAccountArchiveTests` \"decodes every field of the legacy archive\" failed with `sourceUnreadable` (run 44403024224, job 135150903639, the only failure). The replayed legacy archive (`MultisManager.m:49-80`: `NSKeyedArchiver` of an `NSArray` of `NSMutableDictionary` with `NSHTTPCookie`s) does not decode under secure coding with that list. Reverted in `7b2ca13`.\n- **Risk today**: low. The archive comes only from the app's own Keychain item.\n\n### Scope (Mac session)\n\n1. With the replayed archive of `LegacyAccountArchiveTests`, and, if possible, a real `HFR_COMPTES_KEY` written by the legacy app with synthetic accounts (LOT-067 M1), find why secure decoding fails:\n   - which class names the archive holds (`NSKeyedUnarchiver` delegate, or `plutil -p` of the archive's `$objects`/`$classes`);\n   - whether `NSHTTPCookie` adopts `NSSecureCoding`, and which internal classes it decodes.\n2. If a bounded class list decodes it: apply it, keep the legacy test green, and add a test that an archive naming an unexpected class is refused.\n3. If `NSHTTPCookie` cannot decode securely: record that in the LOT-067 spec and close this as not fixable, with the reason.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- The import of the replayed (and, if captured, real) legacy archive stays green on macOS.\n- Either secure decoding with an explicit class list plus a refusal test, or a documented \"cannot\", cited in LOT-067.\n\nRefs #1200, #1202.",
